        "id": "81fea9f1-f7b9-48e2-a30c-b2b96bdae85e",
        "name": "Northroom",
        "description": " As you step inside the Northroom, you are greeted by a burst of frigid air that sends shivers down your spine. The walls are adorned with intricately carved ice sculptures depicting scenes from frozen tundras and icy mountains. A large pile of snow in the corner looks inviting for a snowball fight, but beware - it might not melt anytime soon! In one corner sits a cozy igloo made entirely out of ice blocks, complete with flickering candles providing warm light within. The floor is covered in soft white fur, making you wonder if perhaps some of Santa\u0027s elves have been here before you? On the far end of the room stands an enormous Christmas tree adorned with sparkling icicles and glittering ornaments, casting a magical glow across the entire space.",
